# auferstehung-end - Gustav Mahler, Symphony No. 2 in C minor, the
# finale (fifth movement), its close, about a minute: the chorus's
# "Aufersteh'n, ja aufersteh'n wirst du, mein Herz, in einem Nu!" at 48
# (Pesante, its first eight bars) and the last thirteen bars, 51 ("Noch
# einmal so langsam") to the end. Bars 48+9 to 50+12 are left out.
#
# Source: the first edition of the full score, Leipzig: Friedrich
# Hofmeister, 1897 (University of Toronto copy, Internet Archive
# `symphonieno200mahl`), printed pages 204 (48) and 209 (51 to the end).
# Public domain: published 1897; Mahler died in 1911. Arranged for pax's
# one-voice speaker by its px29 lane; notes/px29-the-chord.md says which
# line is carried where and which bars are not verified.
#
# 48: the sopranos (soprano solo with the chorus), one voice.
# 51: the organ's chord (full organ), bar by bar, as play's arpeggio:
#     bars 1-8 E-flat 3, B-flat 4, E-flat 5, G 5 (the organ also holds
#     E-flat 2 and B-flat 5: one voice carries four); bars 9-12 the
#     organ's upper chord with its added top E-flat 6; the last bar the
#     strings' eighth, sounded with the same four pitches (the strings'
#     own pitches are not all read: see the note).
title Auferstehung, the close (Mahler, Symphony No. 2, 1897)
gap 20
arp 20
order up

# 48 Pesante (quarter = the half before), 4/4
tempo 60
Eb5 2.          # Auf-
Eb5 4           # er-
Eb5 2           # steh'n,
r 4
Eb5 4           # ja
Ab5 2.          # auf-
Ab5 4           # er-
G5 2            # steh'n
r 4
G5 4            # wirst
F5 2            # du,
Eb5 2           # mein
Bb5 2           # Herz,
G5 2            # in
Eb5 4           # ei-
Eb5 4
D5 4            # -nem
Eb5 4
F5 2.+8         # Nu!
r 8

